Texture pack: decide once, at creation (2026-09-11)

A texture's "pack or not" decision is taken once, when its D3D12 resource is
created and sized, and stored on the texture (D3D12Texture::SetTexpackReplacement).
The upload and the view read it from there. Before this each of the three did
its own lookup, and a pack switch (F9) between creation and upload made the
upload read a replacement's rows into a buffer sized for the guest texture: a
heap overrun on the GPU thread (access violation in memcpy under
std::istream::read; on other runs the 0xC0000409 fast-fail of a corrupted
heap). Also: the upload checks the resource fits the replacement before
reading, and the plugin publishes the game's own frame rate as the cvar
guest_fps_x10 for the app's on-screen counter.

Apply from the rexglue-src root:  git apply ../fable2recomp/patches/rexglue-texpack-created-once.patch

